    "Load: other agents were building and testing on the machine throughout (Windows load 28-70 %, a Vite dev server and Chrome sessions of theirs), so every comparison here is an interleaved A/B (before, after, before, after …) and is reported as the median with its min and max. Single slow frames and the absolute 4× figures are less certain than on a calm machine.",
    "Browser: headless Chrome 154 over CDP, the production build served by .cache/perf-fix/harness/serve.mjs (text gzip-compressed, as GitHub Pages sends it), 1366 × 768 at DPR 1.5, the minimap style, the harness of .cache/map-ui-build/harness (atl9.mjs, unchanged in what it measures). selectionToPaintMs / editToPaintMs: from the pointerdown to the frame after the last map call within the quiet period; lastMapCall: when that call ended. 10k-x4: the 10,000-step project of UR.2b at 4×, five drags and a long drag at the zone band.",
    "Node: the benches bundled with esbuild (as vite build bundles) and run interleaved, HEAD then tree, five pairs; the --check verdicts are the committed commands under tsx."
