  "profiles": {
    "$comment": "CPU profiles (CDP Profiler, 100-200 µs sampling) of unminified production builds of eff4341 and of the tree, and node --cpu-prof of the bundled benches; the figures are the profiles' own and are slower than the minified build.",
    "selectionChange": "Node, 10,000 steps: 97 % of a selection change was the spawn layers collected again for the new focus (mergeGroups 0.5 ms, a marker per point, the id sort), the active split re-scanning every piece (0.25 ms) and the focus pan's re-rank. Now: the points before the focus are kept per input and the layers keyed on the groups a focus holds; a selection that focuses none of a layer's groups leaves it untouched.",
    "moveStep": "Node: the drawn route renumbered in a 10,000-entry map at every edit (0.75 ms), every step id hashed for the route pieces (about 1 ms), the split, and a positions map rebuilt for the focus check of an insert. Now incremental.",
    "selectionToMap1x": "Browser, eff4341: the pins waited for the 60 ms settle (UI-04), then the quest-state task (12-21 ms unminified at 1×). Now after the next paint for a still selection.",
    "editToMap1x": "Browser: the edit's React render (10-13 ms), the frame, the walk's zero-delay timer, then the quest state in a task of its own. Now the quest state runs in the walk's task after a quick walk (≤ 8 ms). Tried and withdrawn: walking before the edit's first frame (a microtask) made everything paint in one frame at about 50 ms, but moved the edit's own first paint from about 25 ms to about 50 ms (unminified, 1×).",
    "pans10k4x": "Browser, 4×, unminified, 5 drags: eff4341 ran 16 map syncs, p50 40 ms, most of them walking-path passes issued every 250 ms while dragging (each a full 10,000-step route walk, pathOf 144 ms of 590 ms in all). The tree: 8 syncs, none during a drag; pathOf 40 ms. The post-drag work is the view's sync (Leaflet adding and removing the re-ranked step markers, about 20 ms of it) and one paths pass.",
    "firstArt4x": "Browser, 4×, unminified, cold, 50 Mbit/s (tree): the workspace is ready at about 1.2 s; React's first render and commit take about 620 ms (390 ms of layout effects, a re-render set off by the map region's width measurement in MapPanel, src/ui); the map's mount and route fit about 430 ms. The index arrives at 1.28 s but its reader's continuation runs only after those tasks. The reader chunk now loads with the index (requested at 1.25 s, not 2.25 s), and each sync sends the tile band before building any other layer.",
    "clusterWarm": "Node: every level of every map for the quests open by race and class (908 groups, 959 points): 3.6 ms median (2.2-7.2), in the quest-state task."
  },
